  "term": "tentorium cerebelli",
  "definition": "The tentorium cerebelli is a fold of dura mater that separates the occipital parts of the cerebrum from the cerebellum. It also divides the cranial cavity into upper and lower compartments and helps support brain stability within the skull.",
